'''''Kniphofia uvaria''''' is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Asphodelaceae]], commonly known as '''tritomea''', '''torch lily''', or '''red hot poker''', due to the shape and color of its [[inflorescence]]. The leaves are reminiscent of a lily, and the flowerhead can reach up to {{convert|1.5|m|ft|0|abbr=on}} in height. There are many varieties of torch lily, and they bloom at different times during the growing season. The flowers are red, orange, and yellow.

==Distribution==
''Kniphofia uvaria'' originates from the [[Cape Province]] of [[South Africa]],<ref name=qg-weed /> and has been introduced into many parts of the world, such as [[North America]], [[Australia]], [[New Zealand]], [[Patagonia]] and [[Europe]] as a garden plant. It is hardy in [[Hardiness zone|zones 5–10]].

In parts of south-eastern Australia, such as the [[Central Tablelands|Central]] and [[Southern Tablelands]] of [[New South Wales]] and southern [[Victoria (Australia)|Victoria]], it has [[escaped plant|escaped cultivation]] and become [[Naturalisation (biology)|naturalised]].<ref name=qg-weed>{{cite web|title=Factsheet: Red hot poker – ''Kniphofia uvaria''|url=http://keyserver.lucidcentral.org/weeds/data/03030800-0b07-490a-8d04-0605030c0f01/media/Html/Kniphofia_uvaria.htm|work=Weeds of Australia: Biosecurity Queensland Edition|publisher=[[Queensland Government]]|accessdate=10 February 2012|year=2011|archive-date=12 March 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160312000928/http://keyserver.lucidcentral.org/weeds/data/03030800-0b07-490a-8d04-0605030c0f01/media/Html/Kniphofia_uvaria.htm|url-status=dead}}</ref> It is now regarded as an [[environmental weed]] in these locations, spreading from former habitations into natural areas, where it can grow in thick clumps and threaten sensitive ecosystems. Elsewhere in southern Australia it is regarded as a potential environmental weed, and it may have also naturalised in parts of [[South Australia]] and [[California]].<ref name=qg-weed /> It is also seen in the [[Kumaon division|Kumaon]] Himalayas of India, probably brought during British colonial rule. 

